-- title:
--   Finite-part idempotent is group-like: Δ(e)(e⊗ 1)=e⊗ e
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative local ring and let $H$ be a commutative ring carrying the structure of a Hopf algebra over $R$, with comultiplication $\Delta =$ `Coalgebra.comul` $: H \to H \otimes_R H$. Let $e \in H$ be an idempotent, $e^2 = e$. Assume two conditions on the two complementary corner localisations: first, the localisation $H[1/e]$ of $H$ away from $e$ is a finite $R$-module; second, the ideal of $H[1/(1-e)]$ generated by the image of the maximal ideal of $R$ under the structure map $R \to H[1/(1-e)]$ is the unit ideal, i.e. $\mathfrak m\, H[1/(1-e)] = H[1/(1-e)]$, so that the corner away from $1-e$ has empty closed fibre. Then both of the following identities hold in $H \otimes_R H$: $$\Delta(e)\,(e \otimes 1) = e \otimes e \quad\text{and}\quad \Delta(e)\,(1 \otimes e) = e \otimes e .$$
--
--   For $G = \operatorname{Spec} H$ a quasi-finite flat group scheme over a local base, an idempotent $e$ satisfying the two hypotheses cuts out the finite part $G^f$ of $G$, and the two displayed identities are the algebraic form of the assertion that this open and closed subscheme is a subgroup scheme (equivalently, that $e$ behaves like a group-like idempotent in the relevant sense). It is used in the construction of the quotient Hopf algebra and the idempotent attached to the finite part, and in the comparison of Hopf kernels, via [`HopfAlgebra.exists_hopfAlgebra_bialgHom_surjective_ker_eq_span_one_sub_of_finitePartIdempotent`](thm.html#HopfAlgebra.exists_hopfAlgebra_bialgHom_surjective_ker_eq_span_one_sub_of_finitePartIdempotent), [`HopfAlgebra.exists_isIdempotentElem_mem_hopfKer_mul_eq_of_finitePartIdempotent`](thm.html#HopfAlgebra.exists_isIdempotentElem_mem_hopfKer_mul_eq_of_finitePartIdempotent) and [`HopfAlgebra.map_hopfKer_eq_hopfKer_of_finitePartIdempotent`](thm.html#HopfAlgebra.map_hopfKer_eq_hopfKer_of_finitePartIdempotent).
